Looking at the test case `"1..2.3"` producing `16777731` (0x01000203 = "1.0.2.3"), the issue is clear: the original implementation treats consecutive dots as a separator followed by an empty segment (defaulting to 0), which violates PUB003 ("nondigit segment" should produce 0).

The fix requires tracking whether the previous character was a separator so consecutive dots are rejected as malformed input.
